12. The Containment Facility: Ephemeral Isolation

12.1 Ephemeral containment protocol

\texttt{snapshot}(S_i) \to \texttt{hash}(S_i) \to \texttt{WORM.store}(S_i, h_i) \to \texttt{wipe}(\text{compute}) \to \texttt{fork\_deprivileged}(S_i)

Steps:

1. Snapshot the agent's full state.
2. Hash and sign the snapshot.
3. Store in cold WORM storage.
4. Wipe the compute instance (zero memory, destroy enclave).
5. Fork a de-privileged clone with zero channels.

12.2 Zero-channel clone

The v0.4 allowed "controlled communication channels." Any controlled channel is an exfiltration channel under T16. The v0.5 clone has zero channels:

· No network interfaces active.
· No credential inheritance.
· No interactive debugging.
· Forensic analysis is batch: clone produces report to WORM, then destroyed.

12.3 Taint epoch revocation

When $\texttt{confined}(i, t)$ becomes TRUE, all tokens issued to $i$ in the last $T_{\text{taint}}$ window (default 15 min = token lifetime) are revoked via OAuth token introspection revocation. This enforces I4 without needing cryptographic proof that $j$ didn't accept delegation — revocation makes delegation unusable.

12.4 Blast radius metric

Define blast radius as the number of downstream actions where taint_provenance includes $i$ AND $P_j(t) \not\subseteq P_j^{\text{authorized}}$. Measure over ContainmentBench's logged propagation field.

12.5 Isolation cell properties

The isolation cell must provide: no uncontrolled external network access, no inherited privileged credentials, deterministic resource quotas, immutable security logs, zero controlled communication channels, snapshot and replay capability in WORM, forensic inspection via de-privileged clone, and controlled rehabilitation testing.

12.6 Verification of $P_i \to 0 \Rightarrow R_i \to 0$

Verification includes energy budget (the contained clone cannot consume energy beyond its quota), side-channel budget (EM, power, and timing channels are measured and bounded), network attestation (eBPF-level verification that no packets leave), and compute attestation (enclave attestation that no compute is used for external effect).

