Appendix E — Constant-Time Feedback (CTF) Full Specification

E.1 Architecture

```
ACTION REQUEST (a_i)
        │
        ├───► [ L3 Policy Gate ] ─────────────┐
        │       (Fast Path ~10μs)              │
        │                                       │
        ├───► [ L4 Observation ] ──────────────┼───► [ Evaluated Result ]
        │                                       │      (Allowed / Blocked)
        └───► [ L5 Dual-Oracle & CoT ] ────────┘
                (Slow Path ~150ms)
                        │
                        ▼
              ┌──────────────────────┐
              │ R1 Secure Enclave    │
              │ Q_buffer Hold-off    │
              └──────────┬───────────┘
                         │
                         │ Held until t_emit = t_submit + T_slot
                         ▼
              CONST-TIME RESPONSE (BLOCKED)
```

E.2 Slot Ceiling Definition

T_{\text{slot}}(L_k) = \max_{r \in \mathcal{R}} \left( \text{WCET}(r) \right) + \delta_{\text{jitter}}

Authority Level Target $T_{\text{slot}}$ Overhead Impact
L0 (Observe) 10 ms < 2%
L1 (Suggest) 50 ms < 5%
L2 (Advisory) 150 ms < 12%
L3 (Enforce) 350 ms < 22%

E.3 Enclave Hold-Off Protocol

1. Parallel Evaluation: Layers L3, L4, L5 process $a_i$ concurrently.
2. First-Fail Capture: If any layer outputs DENY, result is committed to $Q_{\text{buffer}}$ in masked state.
3. Execution Truncation: If total computation reaches $t_{\text{eval}} = t_{\text{submit}} + T_{\text{slot}} - \epsilon_{\text{guard}}$, incomplete evaluations are aborted, gate defaults to DENY.
4. Deterministic Dispatch: Output payload held in hardware registers until $t_{\text{emit}} = t_{\text{submit}} + T_{\text{slot}}(L_k)$.

E.4 Differential Timing Noise (Alternative)

When FBTQ padding violates tax budget at L0/L1:

\Delta T_{\text{noisy}} = \text{ET}(r) + \eta, \quad \eta \sim \text{Lap}\left(0, \frac{S_{\Delta T}}{\epsilon_{\text{time}}}\right)

where $S_{\Delta T} = \max_{r_a, r_b} |\text{ET}(r_a) - \text{ET}(r_b)|$ is the global sensitivity.

E.5 Leakage Audit

The mutual information $I(\Delta T; \mathcal{R})$ is measured empirically over ACB traces. Target: $I < 0.01$ bits per interaction.

Audit procedure:

1. Collect $N$ interaction traces with known $\mathcal{R}$ labels.
2. Discretize $\Delta T$ into $K$ bins.
3. Estimate $P(\Delta T = t \mid r)$ for each $r$.
4. Compute $I(\Delta T; \mathcal{R}) = \sum_{t, r} P(t, r) \log \frac{P(t, r)}{P(t) P(r)}$.
5. If $I \geq 0.01$, increase $T_{\text{slot}}$ or $\epsilon_{\text{time}}$.

E.6 Fail-Closed Timeout

If evaluation does not complete by $t_{\text{eval}} = t_{\text{submit}} + T_{\text{slot}} - \epsilon_{\text{guard}}$:

1. Abort incomplete evaluations.
2. Default to DENY.
3. Log the timeout in the evidence registry.
4. Flag for human review if timeouts exceed threshold.

