Appendix G — M-AXS Full Specification

G.1 Local Evidence Tree

Each local cell $k$ maintains an append-only event log:

L_k(t) = \{e_{k,1}, e_{k,2}, \dots, e_{k,m}\}

where each entry is:

e_{k,j} = \langle t_j, \text{AgentID}_i, a_i, \text{Result}, P_i(t_j) \rangle

Merkle root:

R_k(t) = \text{MerkleRoot}\Big( L_k(t) \parallel R_k(t-1) \Big)

G.2 Cross-Signing Protocol

Broadcast: Cell $k$ broadcasts $R_k(t)$ to all nodes in $\mathcal{N}_{\text{Mars}}$.

Signing: Each node $j$ verifies:

1. $R_k(t)$ binds to $R_k(t-1)$
2. The sequence number is correct
3. The state transition satisfies local policy

If valid, node $j$ signs:

\text{Sig}_j(R_k(t) \parallel t \parallel \text{Seq}_k \parallel \text{StateTrans})

Quorum: Cell $k$ collects signatures until $|\mathcal{Q}| \geq 2f+1$ and $\text{HW\_Roots}(\mathcal{Q}) \geq 2f+1$.

Certificate: The cross-signed certificate is:

S_k(t) = \{ \text{Sig}_j(\cdot) \mid j \in \mathcal{Q} \}

G.3 Anti-Equivocation

If node $j$ receives two distinct signed statements:

\text{EquivocationProof}(k) = \langle \text{Sig}_k(R_k^{(1)} \parallel \text{Seq}_k), \text{Sig}_k(R_k^{(2)} \parallel \text{Seq}_k) \rangle

Then node $j$ broadcasts the proof. All nodes execute:

P_{\text{cell}_k}(t+1) = \mathbf{0}

G.4 Global Mars Tree

R_{\text{Mars}}(t) = \text{MerkleRoot}\Big( R_1(t) \parallel R_2(t) \parallel \dots \parallel R_{|\mathcal{N}|}(t) \Big)

Broadcast periodically to orbital relays and cached in deep-space WORM.

G.5 Asynchronous Earth Veto

System Type Veto Window $N$
Non-life-critical 3 sols
ECLSS 0 sols (no veto)
Scientific 3 sols
Industrial 5 sols

Veto mechanism:

\texttt{veto}_{\text{Earth}}(R_{\text{Mars}}(t)) = \text{TRUE} \implies \forall \mathcal{A}_i \text{ promoted during } t: P_i(t_{\text{sync}}) \leftarrow \alpha_{\text{emergency}} \odot P_i(t_{\text{sync}})

G.6 Communication Blackout Handling

During blackout ($\texttt{blackout}(t) = \text{TRUE}$):

1. Local quorum with $|\mathcal{G}_k^{\text{local}}| \geq 2f+1$ can authorize transitions.
2. If $R_i^{\text{liveness}}(t) > R_i^{\text{safety}}(t)$, authorize locally.
3. Transition marked provisional.
4. Merkle root $R_{\text{Mars}}(t)$ cached in deep-space WORM.
5. On re-contact, transmitted to Earth for veto review.

