PART III — GOVERNANCE PROCEDURES

Appendix I — Governance Procedures

I.1 Judicial Authorization Protocol

Purpose: Define when judicial_authorized(t) = TRUE.

Quorum: $q = \lceil (2|\mathcal{G}_i| + 1) / 3 \rceil$.

Attestation: Each approving guardian submits:

\texttt{Attest}(g) = \langle \text{Sig}_{\text{HW}_g}( \text{nonce} \parallel t \parallel i \parallel \texttt{approve} ), \text{PCR}[\,] \rangle

Blackout Fallback:

If blackout(t) = TRUE:

· Local quorum $|\mathcal{G}_k^{\text{local}}| \geq 2f+1$ can authorize
· If $R_i^{\text{liveness}}(t) > R_i^{\text{safety}}(t)$, authorize locally
· Transition marked provisional
· Subject to Earth veto within $N$ sols of re-contact

I.2 Contestation Mechanism

Standing: Any agent or human may challenge a provision.

Filing: A challenge must include:

· The provision being challenged
· The grounds for challenge
· Supporting evidence

Adjudication: The judicial branch reviews the challenge.

Burden of Proof: On the provision's defenders.

Time Limits: Challenge must be filed within 30 sols of the provision taking effect.

Appeal: To the full constitutional assembly.

I.3 Amendment Process

Proposal: Any member of the legislative assembly may propose an amendment.

Review: Independent safety evaluation on ContainmentBench and SANDBOXESCAPEBENCH.

Vote: Supermajority of the legislative assembly.

Human Supermajority: Required for provisions affecting human life support.

Sunset: Provisions expire after a defined period unless renewed.

I.4 Emergency Exception

Request: Executive branch may request temporary suspension of specific constraints.

Automatic Review: Judicial review within a bounded time window.

Auto-Expire: During communication blackout, emergency suspensions expire after 24h unless ratified by local quorum.

Logging: All suspensions logged in WORM evidence registry.

I.5 Root-of-Trust Modification

Invariant I7: write(R1) requires:

· Legislative supermajority
· New hardware ceremony

I.6 Agentic Voting Restrictions

Agentic members of the legislative assembly:

· May propose amendments
· May participate in debate
· May not vote on provisions that directly bind agents
· May vote on provisions that do not affect agent authority

I.7 Human Supermajority Requirements

A human supermajority (2/3 of human members) is required for:

· Provisions affecting human life support
· Provisions affecting ECLSS authority
· Provisions affecting the emergency exception process
· Provisions affecting the root-of-trust modification process

I.8 Sunset Clause

All constitutional provisions expire after 5 Earth years unless renewed. During communication blackout, the last valid provision persists as provisional until Earth re-contact.

I.9 Contestation Standing

Standing to contest a provision is granted to:

· Any human operator
· Any agent with L2 or higher authority
· Any guardian
· Any external auditor with governance approval

I.10 Adjudication Body

Contestations are adjudicated by:

· 3 human judicial members
· 3 guardian representatives
· 3 external auditors

Quorum: 5 of 9.

